cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark dataset in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "BharatPII: Multilingual, Perturbation-Aware Benchmark for Personally Identifiable Information Extraction in Indian Contexts"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
keywords:
  - "Personally Identifiable Information"
  - "Indian Languages"
  - "Information Extraction"
  - "Adversarial Robustness"
  - "Benchmark"
  - "Named Entity Recognition"
  - "Synthetic PII"
abstract: >-
  BharatPII is a standardized evaluation benchmark for Personally Identifiable
  Information (PII) extraction under Indian linguistic variation and adversarial
  perturbations. Covering 964 canonical evaluation records with 724 gold standard
  Indian PII entities across 8 categories, 5 Indic language and script regimes,
  and 5 adversarial perturbation families (A1–A5), accompanied by 1,200 disjoint
  adaptation instances.
